+# smallpt — browser edition
+
+Kevin Beason's open-source C++ path tracer compiled to WebAssembly. Open `index.html` through static hosting. Rendering runs entirely on the client in a module worker; no backend or cross-origin isolation is required.
+
+- **Randomize & render** changes the wall, mirror, and glass reflectances and starts a fresh render.
+- Quality and resolution controls restart the render with the current palette.
+- Reset restores the original Cornell-box colors. The download button exports the canvas as PNG.
+- A bundled render from the same WASM module is shown during initialization.
+
+## Build
+
+Compiled `assets/smallpt.mjs` and `assets/smallpt.wasm` are included. `npm run build` copies the static application into `dist` without requiring Emscripten.
+
+To recompile the C++, install Emscripten and run `npm run build:wasm`. `npm test` executes the WASM directly in Node and checks rendered pixels, repeatability, color changes, and progressive accumulation.
+
+`vendor/smallpt/smallpt.cpp` is the unmodified upstream source from https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/smallpt.txt. Its MIT license is retained in `vendor/smallpt/LICENSE.txt`. `native/browser.cpp` replaces file output and OpenMP with an exported RGBA framebuffer, progressive 2×2-subpixel sampling, and palette controls. The original radiance, intersection, material, and camera calculations are retained.
+
+No browser QA or preview/dev server was used for this implementation.
